{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) issued stitch task #5538 to implement `cmd/truncate/main.go` - the core file size operations for the `truncate` utility. The task is scoped to srd083-truncate requirements R1.1 through R1.4 only (not R2 reference file or full R3 exit codes). The specific requirements are:\n   - R1.1: Parse `--size=SIZE` / `-s SIZE` with unit suffix support (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for 1024; KB, MB, GB for 1000)\n   - R1.2: Support SIZE prefixes: `+` (grow), `-` (shrink), `<` (at most), `>` (at least), `/` (round down to multiple), `%` (round up to multiple)\n   - R1.3: Process multiple FILE arguments with the same size operation\n   - R1.4: `-c` / `--no-create` suppresses file creation for nonexistent files; without `-c`, missing files are created\n   \n   Design decisions: use `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, use `pkg/sizeparse` for SIZE parsing, use `os.Truncate` for resizing, match GNU truncate exit codes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Manual CLI argument parsing (no cobra for cmd/ utilities - following stat/main.go pattern)\n   - `pkg/sizeparse.ParseWithOptions()` for parsing size strings with unit suffixes and sign prefixes\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - `os.Truncate()` for setting file sizes\n   - Differential testing pattern against GNU reference binary (`gtruncate`)\n   - File creation with `os.Create()` for nonexistent files (unless `--no-create`)\n   - Relative size adjustments with `+`, `-`, `<`, `>`, `/`, `%` prefixes on SIZE\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml`\n     - The full SRD defining all requirements for truncate\n     - Key: R1.1-R1.4 (scoped for this task), R2 (reference file - not in scope), R3 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no sparse file optimization\n     - Package contract imports: `pkg/sizeparse` and `pkg/sys`\n   \n   - `cmd/stat/main.go` (reference pattern for implementation)\n     - Shows the manual arg parsing pattern used across cmd/ utilities\n     - Key patterns: `parseArgs()` → `(options, []string, error)`, `run()` → `int` exit code, `parseLongFlag()`, `parseShortFlags()`\n     - Full code at 224 lines showing options struct, help/version text, error formatting\n\n   - `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go` (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - `Parse(s string) (int64, error)` - basic parsing\n     - `ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)` - with `AllowSign bool` and `DefaultUnit int64`\n     - Supports suffixes: b(512), K/KiB(1024), KB(1000), M/MiB, MB, G/GiB, GB, T, P, E and overflow suffixes Z, Y\n     - `splitParts()` handles `+`/`-` sign prefix when `AllowSign=true`\n     - NOTE: sizeparse only handles `+`/`-` signs. The `<`, `>`, `/`, `%` prefixes from R1.2 need custom handling in truncate itself.\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided in project_context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main()\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Was in the research/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that `pkg/sizeparse` handles `+`/`-` but NOT `<`, `>`, `/`, `%` prefixes. The truncate implementation needs to strip these prefixes before calling sizeparse, then apply the operation semantics after getting the numeric value.\n   - The approach should be: parse the SIZE string to extract the operation prefix (if any), pass the remaining numeric+suffix portion to `sizeparse.ParseWithOptions`, then apply the operation (exact set, relative grow/shrink, at-most, at-least, round-down, round-up) when truncating each file.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The complete stitch task prompt with all project context, SRDs, source code, requirements, constraints, and instructions for implementing cmd/truncate/main.go\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/truncate/main.go` implementing srd083 R1.1-R1.4\n   - Verify compilation with `go build ./cmd/truncate/`\n   - Verify `go vet ./cmd/truncate/` passes\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC5\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two reference files (srd083-truncate.yaml and cmd/stat/main.go) and was about to write `cmd/truncate/main.go`. I had completed the planning phase:\n   - Understood the SRD requirements (R1.1-R1.4 in scope)\n   - Studied the stat/main.go pattern for argument parsing\n   - Identified that sizeparse handles numeric+suffix parsing but custom prefix handling (`<`, `>`, `/`, `%`) is needed\n   - Was ready to write the implementation file\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/truncate/main.go` following the patterns from `cmd/stat/main.go`. The implementation needs:\n   - Copyright header\n   - Manual arg parsing for `-s`/`--size=SIZE`, `-c`/`--no-create`, `--help`, `--version`, `--` end-of-flags\n   - SIZE parsing: strip operation prefix (`+`, `-`, `<`, `>`, `/`, `%`), call `sizeparse.ParseWithOptions` with `AllowSign=false` (since we handle the prefix ourselves), apply the operation to determine final file size\n   - For each FILE: if not exists and no-create is set, skip; if not exists, create it; then truncate to computed size using `os.Truncate`\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   \n   This directly continues the task from the user's prompt: \"Implement cmd/truncate core file size operations (srd083 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-va